  "notes": "{薄|うす}める means to make a liquid less concentrated by adding water or another substance. Can also be used figuratively for weakening an impression or effect.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {薄|うす}まる (intransitive — becomes diluted on its own)\n- Pattern: XをYで{薄|うす}める (dilute X with Y)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{薄|うす}めている means 'is in the process of diluting' (ongoing action).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {水|みず}で{薄|うす}める: to dilute with water\n- {薄|うす}めて{使|つか}う: to use in diluted form\n- {薄|うす}めた{液|えき}: diluted solution\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {薄|うす}い: thin, weak, light (base adjective)\n- {薄|うす}まる: to become diluted (intransitive pair)\n- {濃|こ}い: thick, concentrated (opposite quality)",
